From 01fb47dd60de85e819a6dd34d3e7db5ae0543b5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Red Daka <emmanuel.rayan.daka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 05:58:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix dead-end Gallery link; translate
 Collection/Gallery/Shop/About
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes a real broken-feeling link, not a content decision: /collection's
footer always linked to "View full gallery →", but gallery_photos has
zero rows (confirmed earlier — every photo you've uploaded went to
Collection instead, gallery_photos and collection_items are otherwise
identical in schema/RLS). Added a lightweight count-only query
(select head:true, count:exact) and made the link conditional on
Gallery actually having published photos, so it never points visitors
at an empty page regardless of which way the underlying Collection-vs-
Gallery content question eventually goes.

Translates the four static/simple public pages first, as a complete
verified slice — Collection, Gallery, Shop, About. All hardcoded
English replaced with useTranslation() calls; both locale dictionaries
extended with common.*, collection.*, gallery.*, shop.*, and about.*
namespaces.

Caught and fixed a real bug while doing this: collection.tsx's tile
grid used `.map((t) => ...)` with the map parameter also named `t`,
which shadowed useTranslation()'s `t` function inside that scope.
`t("common.video")` inside the callback was therefore trying to call a
Tile object, not translate a string — tsc caught this immediately
("This expression is not callable"). Renamed the map (and a `.find`
with the same collision) to `tile`/`tile.id` rather than aliasing the
translation function, keeping the `const { t } = useTranslation()`
convention consistent with every other translated file this session.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean on all four files (running
--fix on them also cleaned up pre-existing Prettier debt they already
had before this commit — project-wide error count actually dropped,
1290 to 1243). vite build succeeds; confirmed the Japanese dictionary
is present in the shipped client bundle. Live dev server checks confirm
all four pages render their translated English text correctly with no
raw i18n keys leaking, and that the Gallery link no longer renders
unconditionally.

Not yet translated, for a follow-up pass: Settings, Auth, Newsletter,
Show, the story/diary/dear-today list and detail pages, and the entire
admin/Studio panel — the bulk of the "system wide" scope, deferred
deliberately to ship this as a complete, verified piece rather than a
half-done pass across everything.
